      "consent_info_title": "How the Consent Ledger Works",
      "consent_info_text": "Every time a consent request is created, approved, or rejected, the app saves a permanent, time-stamped record of it — and links it to the record right before it, like a chain of receipts where each new one carries a copy of the one before. If anyone ever tried to sneak in a fake entry, delete one, or quietly change what happened afterward, the chain wouldn't match up anymore, and the app would notice right away and show a warning here. This means your consent history can't be secretly altered after the fact, giving you a reliable, tamper-evident record of every decision made about your care."
    },
